        "content": "<p>adamrk opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15041\">PR #15041</a> from <code>adamrk:abk/cleanup-run_http-test-helper</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The <code>run_http</code> test helper currently takes a channel and sends the uncollected http request down that channel for the caller to see. But only a few tests actually use that and it can otherwise be difficult because the request body many never actually be read and a guest program can be left hanging if it awaits that.</p>\n<p>This change hopefully makes <code>run_http</code> more intuitive by not taking the channel and in general reading the full request body. The new version <code>run_http_get_forwarded_request</code> can be used if the caller needs to see how the request was passed along and the new endpoint <code>p3-test-immediate-response</code> can be used when the test needs a response to be sent without the body being read.</p>\n<p>&lt;!--<br>\nPlease make sure you include the following information:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>If this work has been discussed elsewhere, please include a link to that<br>\n  conversation. If it was discussed in an issue, just mention \"issue #...\".</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain why this change is needed. If the details are in an issue already,<br>\n  this can be brief.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Our development process is documented in the Wasmtime book:<br>\n<a href=\"https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html\">https://docs.wasmtime.dev/contributing-development-process.html</a></p>\n<p>Please review the Bytecode Alliance's AI tool usage policy at<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/governance/blob/main/AI_TOOL_POLICY.md</a></p>\n<p>Please ensure all communication follows the code of conduct:<br>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a><br>\n--&gt;</p>\n</blockquote>",
